{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795628805","published":"2026-11-25T17:46:58Z","modified":"2026-11-26T07:45:11.067578509Z","upstream":["CVE-2022-41409","CVE-2026-103111","CVE-2026-86145","CVE-2026-89161"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2022-41409, CVE-2026-103111, CVE-2026-86145, CVE-2026-89161","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop in pcre2test on a negative repeat count\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2022-41409.patch: reject a zero or negative repeat\n       value in a subject line in src/pcre2test.c.\n     - CVE-2022-41409\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write in the DFA matcher workspace\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-86145.patch: check that a reused workspace\n       block is large enough and clamp a new block to the remaining heap\n       limit without overflow in more_workspace() in src/pcre2_dfa_match.c.\n     - CVE-2026-86145\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: invalid free after JIT fast path matching\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-89161.patch: free a previously copied subject\n       and clear PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT in pcre2_jit_match() in\n       src/pcre2_jit_match.c.\n     - CVE-2026-89161\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write on large JIT stack allocations\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-103111.patch: grow the JIT stack enough to\n       cover allocations larger than half the growth rate in\n       src/pcre2_jit_compile.c.\n     - CVE-2026-103111","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-16-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpcre2-16-0?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.34-7ubuntu0.1+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu20.04els/CLSA-2026-1795628805.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpcre2-32-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpcre2-32-0?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.34-7ubuntu0.1+tux